Matthew and Daniel,

I've attached the issued decision BRT-CD-20260818-001 for tomorrow's reconcil=
iation shadow window, 09:00=E2=80=9309:30 UTC. This permits read-only compari=
son for up to 10% of eligible jobs; it does not authorise writes or postings.

Matthew, please confirm the preflight before starting: the normal worker pool=
 and matching workload mix, the no-write/no-post check and at least 25% headr=
oom. You own the start and stop decision. Stop immediately if headroom falls =
below 25%, if there is any output discrepancy, or if there is a customer-faci=
ng regression. Daniel will watch the trailing 15-minute p95 against the verif=
ied 2,800/min ceiling.

Claire, the existing customer path will stay unchanged. The normal reconcilia=
tion release and the next Faregate rollout tranche remain on hold.

Daniel, please bring the observations, or the reason for standing down, to th=
e 11:00 UTC Operations review on 19 August. Any expansion needs my further de=
cision at or after that review.

Thanks,
Anjali


